Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: Allow CPU access to textures that are not render targets or depth buffers.

Applications Lock() video memory textures and write to them, and wined3d's CPU
blitter can only write textures that allow CPU access. Without it uploads fail
with "Operation requires 0x2 access".
---
diff --git a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
index e6ed79a..5369b2d 100644
--- a/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
+++ b/dlls/ddraw/surface.c
@@ -6331,6 +6331,12 @@ static HRESULT ddraw_texture_init(struct ddraw_texture *texture, struct ddraw *d
             WARN("Failed to create draw texture, hr %#lx.\n", hr);
     }
 
+    /* Applications lock video memory textures and write to them directly, and
+     * wined3d's CPU blitter can only write textures that allow CPU access.
+     * Render targets and depth/stencil buffers need to stay GPU only. */
+    if (!(wined3d_desc.bind_flags & (WINED3D_BIND_RENDER_TARGET | WINED3D_BIND_DEPTH_STENCIL)))
+        wined3d_desc.access |= WINED3D_RESOURCE_ACCESS_CPU;
+
     /* Some applications assume surfaces will always be mapped at the same
      * address. Some of those also assume that this address is valid even when
      * the surface isn't mapped, and that updates done this way will be
